pgrep -a - searches running processes by name and prints the PID along with the full command line.

pmap -x PID - displays the memory map of a process with extended details like size, resident memory and dirty pages.

Address - the starting virtual address of each memory region.

Kbytes - the size of the region in virtual memory.

RSS - the part of the region currently in physical RAM (resident set size).

Dirty - the part of the region that has been modified since it was loaded.

Mode - the permissions of the region, where r is read, w is write, x is execute and - means not allowed.

Mapping - what the region belongs to, such as the program file, a library, or anonymous memory.
